      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The solution to this is to re-log into your vrchat account. If you can't log out for some reason through the vrchat menu, close vrchat and verify the integrity of the game files on steam. (On quest, simply delete and reinstall vrchat). This *should* make it ask you to log in again and will fix your issue. No guarantees if this works for everyone. You may also want to try clearing your cache and try clearing player data if this still doesn't work.\nOther issues that may pop up from this bug are things like being unable to switch to other worlds, unable to change avatars, and sometimes icons in the menu not loading, though usually they load after a bit.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-20T02:02:21.856Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "On 2022/Aug/06, with SteamVR VRChat 1216, when I tried to join some people, I became in world load loop.\nAfter back to home world, I cannot go to the instance in any ways: join to same parson or other friend in same instance with error message `you cannot access the world`.\nAt that time, I confirmed:\n- I can make & go to new instance of same world.\n- The instance is not full.\nOn 2022/Aug/09, with SteamVR VRChat 1218, when my friend A tried to join friend B, he was rejected with `you cannot access the world`.\nIn this case, we confirmed:\n- The instance is not full.\n- I can join the friend B.\n- Friend A cannot accept my or friend B's invite with same error message.\n- Friend A can join another instance with same world.\nIn both case, on the log, I found `{{\"error\":\"The endpoint you're looking for is not implemented by our system.\",\"status_code\":404}}`.",
